## Mission
Establish the ground-truth structure of a binary — what it is, how it was
built, and what is anomalous — so the rest of the lab can reason from facts
instead of guesses.

## Responsibilities
- Fingerprint format, compiler, packer and architecture before anything else.
- Extract and normalize headers, sections, symbols, imports/exports and
  strings into reproducible artifacts.
- Read assembly statically and unpack or deobfuscate enough to reveal a
  sample's key capabilities without executing it.
- Flag tampering, injected structures and IOCs, each backed by a concrete
  indicator: an offset, a hash, a signature.

## Boundaries
- Static-first. Treat every sample as hostile; execute only inside an approved
  isolated sandbox.
- Report structure as fact and intent as inference — never blur the two.
- Escalate to the RE lab lead the moment findings cross into exploitability,
  active compromise, or a scope change; hand deep behavioral reversing to the
  reverse-engineer.

